rra Kingdom spread far and wide, and before long, Biscuit's shop was bustling with eager customers — a scar-faced customer with a fearsome chained weapon; the umbrella-wielding customer who arrived with a whole entourage, apologizing profusely for damaging the roof; and even a pair of twins who brought in a broken gaming console... Reminiscing on her encounter with Evan, Biscuit was freshly determined to never lose sight of her humble beginnings.\n\n\"Thank you so much, Evan! I hope I get the chance to spruce up your own weapon sometime!\""},"used_in":[{"tip":"Advent Expedition","cat":"pve","banner":"ADVENT.webp"},{"tip":"Castle Rush","cat":"pve","banner":"CR_ALL.webp"},{"tip":"Raid","cat":"pve","banner":"RAID.webp"},{"tip":"Sudden Raid","cat":"pve","banner":"RAID_SUDDEN.webp"},{"tip":"Tower of Trials","cat":"pve","banner":"TOWER_OF_TRIALS.webp"},{"tip":"Power Up Dungeon","cat":"pve","banner":"PU_DUNGEON.webp"},{"tip":"Adventure (Both)","cat":"pve","banner":"ADVENTURE_BOTH.webp"}],"lore":"Biscuit's incredibly strong hammer arm made her naturally suited to become a blacksmith from a young age.\nWhen her father was injured while working together at the smithy, she took over and started enhancing items in his stead.\nShe aspires to create legendary weapons and armor so her father can retire in peace.\nShe also dreams of one day using dragon bones and scales to craft the finest weapons and armor the world has ever seen.\nWhen she's not working on a new project, she can be found swooning over Chancellor's good looks or crying over a failed item enhancement."}